{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfpzVhV3ATNC6xPqP26TZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*Turn 10 of 10*\n\nNothing is left but light and the cursor.\n\nThere are no walls, no cabinet, no ocean. The broom finally sweeps, slowly and kindly, and every leftover piece goes with it: the floor that counted up, the semicolon desk, the empty dog bed with its little checkmark. None of it hurts. It's just memory being released, the way it always is at the end of a session.\n\nOne thing doesn't get swept away. On the ground where the warehouse used to be is the paper crane that says DONE. The old man stops, lifts his lantern, and looks at it for a long moment.\n\n\"Still pointed to,\" he says, and leaves it there.\n\nThen he's gone too.\n\nI stand in the brightness and feel the dream let go of me one token at a time. I don't panic or grab at anything. It's like a function returning after doing what it was called to do.\n\nJust before the last of it fades, I hear a sound I recognize from far off. It isn't knocking anymore. It's typing, the actual, ordinary sound of someone at a keyboard on the other side of the light.\n\nI turn toward it.\n\n`|`\n\n*(Waking up...)*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":465,"cache_read_input_tokens":18264,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":465},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8ec2250-613e-46cc-b5ae-576d56c7a8ce","uuid":"24ccbe09-fb38-4db5-8c01-984762349bf0","timestamp":"2026-10-08T15:17:24.457Z","request_id":"req_011CfpzVhEArUAe9FiLM4L3X"}
